WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Repetition matters because skill improves through repeated attempts, feedback,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.650
and correction.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.436
A single explanation or demonstration rarely creates reliable performance.

00:00:08.436 --> 00:00:12.340
Repetition gives the learner multiple chances to notice the cue, make the decision,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.320
perform the step, and compare the result.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.420
It also helps parts of the skill become more fluent so attention can move to higher-level

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.160
judgment.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.760
Exact repetition is useful early, but it is not always enough.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.560
If every practice attempt looks the same,

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.300
the learner may memorize the surface pattern without understanding the underlying

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.000
principle.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.940
Variation helps the skill become more flexible.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.800
Change the example, the context, the difficulty, the timing,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.240
or the constraints so the learner has to recognize what matters rather than copy a fixed

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:37.880
script.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.693
Practicing edge cases is especially useful when real work includes ambiguity.

00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:44.237
A strong troubleshooter needs more than the clean example.

00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:46.645
A strong communicator needs more than the friendly audience.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:49.660
A strong analyst needs more than the obvious signal.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.470
Variation teaches the learner how the skill behaves when conditions shift,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.205
evidence is incomplete, or the usual shortcut no longer works.

00:00:56.205 --> 00:00:57.040
Transfer is the goal.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.100
The learner should be able to apply the skill in a different task, context,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.800
or real-world situation.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.215
Retrieval and recall can support that transfer by asking learners to bring back the

00:01:05.215 --> 00:01:07.935
principle without the answer sitting in front of them.

00:01:07.935 --> 00:01:09.360
Repetition builds stability.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.725
Variation builds adaptability.

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:14.120
Together they reduce brittle skill that only works in one familiar scenario.
